1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
You get the tall ships and all of these guns.

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,540
But when the ship goes down and is spotting another vessel,

3
00:00:06,690 --> 00:00:08,670
the entire ship has to turn

4
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:12,090
because the guns are pointing out from the sides of it.

5
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:14,930
So you go forward, you turn, you fire.

6
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:17,510
So, that was done for hundreds of years.

7
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,630
But what made Monitor unique was

8
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,430
it now separated the move into the gun

9
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:24,470
from the movement of the vessel.

10
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,110
So the vessel could be in any orientation.

11
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:29,090
And because Monitor had the world's

12
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:31,310
first revolving gun turret that went into battle,

13
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,250
it was able to move in any direction as well.

14
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:36,670
So that was a huge marker

15
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,670
in the change of these technologies.

16
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,150
And also, we can't forget that it's a transition

17
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:44,230
from that wooden warship, those wooden walls,

18
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:47,970
now iron and metal, which is modern naval warfare.
